message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "QVEX — Quantum Vacuum Exchange Engine"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adelgachkar/QVEX_v0.1.0"
url: "https://github.com/adelgachkar/QVEX_v0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  QVEX (Quantum Vacuum Exchange Engine) is a modular, DAG-based research
  scaffold for coupled optical/photonic cavity simulations, dynamic
  inter-cavity coupling, boundary stress integration, and geometric curvature
  proxies. It provides a deterministic pure-Python graph execution engine,
  registered physics node types, JSON-defined pipelines, and a pytest suite.
  Preliminary/schematic research scaffold; physical mappings are
  phenomenological and require observational fitting before any scientific
  claim.
